{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"The ruling confirms that the counter must be shared across lexical regions and generator resumes, with each site carrying its own threshold. The current lowering still explicitly treats `ticks` as inert, so I’m tracing how statement marks and request state enter the existing execution path before changing it."}}
