{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '6000,6060p' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc; sed -n '6140,6245p' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc; sed -n '4000,4130p' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc; sed -n '30,45p' deps.edn\"","aggregated_output":"(defn- error-exception-members\n  \"ErrorException: Exception's members, the `severity` property, its own\n   constructor and `getSeverity`.\"\n  []\n  (let [m (throwable-members \"Exception\")\n        replace-method (fn [methods e] (conj (vec (remove #(= (:lc %) (:lc e)) methods)) e))\n        entry (fn [mn kind]\n                {:name mn, :lc (str/lower-case mn), :vis :public, :declaring \"ErrorException\",\n                 :final? (not= kind :ee-ctor), :native kind})]\n    (assoc m\n           :props-decl (conj (:props-decl m)\n                             {:name \"severity\", :vis :protected, :declaring \"ErrorException\",\n                              :id \"severity\", :default 1})\n           :methods (-> (:methods m)\n                        (replace-method (entry \"__construct\" :ee-ctor))\n                        (replace-method (entry \"getSeverity\" :severity))))))\n\n\n(def ^:private seed-table\n  \"Name to descriptor, with the lower-cased `:ancestors` the declaration code\n   reads. The Throwable family carries its inherited members.\"\n  (reduce (fn [table [nm kind parent ifaces final?]]\n            (let [lc (str/lower-case nm)\n                  anc (reduce (fn [acc x] (into acc (remove (set acc)) (:ancestors (get table x))))\n                              [lc]\n                              (concat (when parent [parent]) ifaces))\n                  members (if (contains? #{\"Exception\" \"Error\"} nm)\n                            (throwable-members nm)\n                            (if (= nm \"ErrorException\")\n                              (error-exception-members)\n                              (select-keys (get table parent) [:props-decl :methods])))]\n              (assoc table\n                     nm (merge {:php/type :class,\n                                :name nm,\n                                :kind kind,\n                                :parent (or parent :php/null),\n                                :interfaces ifaces,\n                                :traits [],\n                                :ancestors anc,\n                                :abstract? false,\n                                :final? (boolean final?),\n                                :constants [],\n                                :props-decl [],\n                                :static-props [],\n                                :methods [],\n                                :cases [],\n                                :attrs []}\n                               members))))\n          {}\n          seed-classes))\n\n\n(def ^:private define core/define)\n\n\n(defn- constants-form\n  \"The guest map expression seeding `php.rt/constants` from\n   `builtins/constants`, so `defined` and `constant` agree with the\n   lowering's folded literals.\"\n  []\n  (reduce (fn [m [nm v]]\n                [(define 'php.rt/state :php/ready) :php/null])\n              :php/null)))\n\n\n(def definitions\n  \"The single definition list, `[store-key form]` in definition order: every\n   prelude function, the literal state slot, then `php/init!`. Defining them\n   runs nothing.\"\n  (into (into (into core-definitions module-defs/definitions) p9-defs/definitions)\n        [['php.rt/state :php/uninit]\n         ['php/init! (init-form)]]))\n\n\n(defn- definitions->uast\n  [defs]\n  ;; A linear `then` chain adds two tree levels per definition; at this\n  ;; prelude's size the bundled tree runs ~900 deep and overflows the Dart\n  ;; stack in the recursive tree walkers. Balance the sequence, preserving\n  ;; left-to-right effects and the last definition's value.\n  (letfn [(sequence-tree\n            [nodes]\n            (if (<= (count nodes) 1)\n              (first nodes)\n              (let [middle (quot (count nodes) 2)]\n                (u/then (sequence-tree (subvec nodes 0 middle))\n                        (sequence-tree (subvec nodes middle))))))]\n    (sequence-tree (mapv (fn [[k form]] (u/def! k (u/sexp->uast form))) defs))))\n\n\n(def functions-uast\n  \"The bundled shared-call definitions, PHP lambdas and literal state slot.\"\n  (definitions->uast (into call/definitions definitions)))\n\n\n(def uast\n  \"The bundled prelude: every definition, then the task's runtime state\n   allocated by `php/init!`.\"\n  (u/then functions-uast (u/sexp->uast '(php/init!))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The module emitter: the same definition list as the linker module `php`\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def module-name\n  \"The linker module the PHP runtime profile is published as.\"\n  'php)\n\n\n(def runtime-keys\n  \"Every key `php/init!` allocates, the ready flag aside, sorted.\"\n  '[php.rt/class-index php.rt/classes php.rt/cmp-depth php.rt/ctx php.rt/diag php.rt/diag-stream\n    php.rt/error-handler\n    php.rt/error-mask php.rt/error-masks\n    php.rt/class-order php.rt/exception-handler php.rt/exception-handlers php.rt/finalizable php.rt/pending-exc\n    php.rt/shutdown-fns php.rt/exit-status php.rt/in-shutdown php.rt/fatal-escape\n    php.rt/exit-escape php.rt/shutdown-escape php.rt/strict php.rt/included php.rt/path-map php.rt/unit\n    php.rt/autoloaders php.rt/autoloading php.rt/class-map php.rt/constants\n    php.rt/error-reporting php.rt/error-handlers php.rt/functions php.rt/globals php.rt/int-max\n    php.rt/int-min php.rt/next-cell php.rt/next-ord\n    php.rt/out php.rt/request php.rt/response php.rt/response-stream\n    php.rt/headers-sent php.rt/status php.rt/tmps])\n\n\n(defn strip\n  \"`sym` without the module's own namespace `php`; `php.rt/*` stays\n   qualified.\"\n  [sym]\n  (core/strip \"php\" sym))\n\n\n(defn- binder-symbols\n  \"Every symbol a `fn` parameter list or `let` binding vector in `form`\n   binds.\"\n  [form]\n  (cond\n    (and (seq? form) (= 'fn (first form)))\n    (into (set (second form)) (mapcat binder-symbols) (drop 2 form))\n    (and (seq? form) (= 'let (first form)))\n    (into (set (take-nth 2 (second form)))\n          (mapcat binder-symbols)\n          (concat (take-nth 2 (rest (second form))) (drop 2 form)))\n    (coll? form) (into #{} (mapcat binder-symbols) (seq form))\n    :else #{}))\n\n\n(defn- unshadow\n  \"`form` with every local binder named like a module export renamed (`h` to\n   `h%l`): the module emitter strips `php/h` to the bare `h`, which a local\n   `h` would otherwise capture. Globals are qualified before stripping, so\n   every bare occurrence is the local.\"\n  [exports [k form]]\n  (let [clash (set (filter exports (binder-symbols form)))]\n    [k\n     (if (empty? clash)\n       form\n       (walk/postwalk (fn [x] (if (contains? clash x) (symbol (str x \"%l\")) x)) form))]))\n\n\n(def ^:private module-definitions\n  (core/module-definitions\n    \"php\" :php/uninit runtime-keys\n    (mapv (partial unshadow (into #{} (map (fn [[k _]] (strip k))) definitions)) definitions)))\n\n\n(def module-uast\n                 :yang.php/refusal :yang.php/undeclared-free registry\n                 {:name bundle-name,\n                  :ast ast,\n                  :exports (set (mapcat val keys-for)),\n                  :runtime-name prelude/module-name,\n                  :runtime-address php-address,\n                  :deps (into {} (map (fn [[p a]] [(path-module-symbol p) a])) deps)})\n        require-profile (vm/profile-of vm/primitives 'require)]\n    (core-module/scc-module-specs\n      bundle\n      (mapv (fn [{:keys [name]}]\n              (let [[sk bk] (get keys-for name)]\n                (core-module/alias-spec (path-module-symbol name) module-exports\n                                        require-profile bundle-name sk bk)))\n            units))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The lowering stage\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def program-medium\n  \"The program medium's logical identity when the composition names none.\"\n  :yang.php/program)\n\n\n(defn- stage-config\n  \"The shared stage config; `warned` receives the packet's warnings.\"\n  [warned]\n  {:diagnostic-ns diagnostic-ns,\n   :program-medium program-medium,\n   :ok? #(= :yang.cst/ok (:yang.cst/outcome %)),\n   :lower (fn [state packet]\n            (let [{:keys [ast warnings]}\n                  (lower-program packet (select-keys state option-keys))]\n              (reset! warned warnings)\n              ast)),\n   :option-keys option-keys})\n\n\n(defn lower-transform\n  \"The lowering stage's transform (`yang.core.stage/lower-transform`):\n   an ok packet is one program batch, then one record on port `:diagnostics`\n   per warning (`:severity :warning`); a refusal is a diagnostic and no\n   program. Stateless.\"\n  [state packet]\n  (let [warned (atom [])\n        [state' outputs] (core-stage/lower-transform (stage-config warned) state packet)]\n    [state'\n     (into outputs\n           (map (fn [w] [:diagnostics (assoc w :yang.cst/unit (:yang.cst/unit packet))]))\n           @warned)]))\n\n\n(defn open-stage\n  \"A lowering stage reading CST packets from `cst-stream`, writing program\n   batches to `program-stream`, whose logical identity is `medium`, and\n   diagnostics to `diagnostics-stream`. The fourth argument may instead be\n   an options map `{:medium :prelude}`.\"\n  ([cst-stream program-stream diagnostics-stream]\n   (core-stage/open-stage (stage-config (atom [])) cst-stream program-stream diagnostics-stream))\n  ([cst-stream program-stream diagnostics-stream medium-or-opts]\n   (core-stage/open-stage (stage-config (atom []))\n                          cst-stream\n                          program-stream\n                          diagnostics-stream\n                          medium-or-opts)))\n\n\n(defn step-stage\n  [s]\n  (stage/step s lower-transform))\n                           :main-opts [\"-m\" \"btree-bench\"]}\n           :test {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                  :extra-deps {io.github.cognitect-labs/test-runner\n                               {:git/tag \"v0.5.1\" :git/sha \"dfb30dd\"}\n                               ;; latte-kernel: the LaTTe proof assistant's kernel,\n                               ;; the differential oracle for the yang.clojure gap\n                               ;; program (pinned; MIT; dependency-free)\n                               latte-kernel/latte-kernel\n                               {:git/url \"https://github.com/latte-central/latte-kernel\"\n                                :git/sha \"86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279\"}}\n                  ;; The guest recursion limit allows depth that needs more than the\n                  ;; JVM's platform default thread stack (1024 KB on Linux, 2048 KB on\n                  ;; macOS): under 1 MB the guard loses to a JVM StackOverflowError\n                  ;; before it can raise Python's RecursionError, so the same tests\n                  ;; pass on macOS and fail on Linux. 4 MB is twice the measured\n                  ;; macOS-default minimum, leaving headroom as the prelude grows.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
